  "title": "Atrophy’s Eden",
  "subtitle": "A Gothic Literature Audio Drama",
  "description": "London, 1897. Sebastian Moran has an unusual employer, but you can't really be picky about work in this day and age. Being in the employment of James Moriarty is an exercise in patience - strange requests, jobs no sniper in his right mind would ever take - all without so much as an explanation. He won't have to endure alone much longer, though... Moriarty is assembling a team of the best criminals money can buy: a charismatic thief, an insane ex-murderer, a abomination of science, an utterly godless man, and the world's leading vampire scholar. This tribute to classic literature employs an almost League of Extraordinary Gentleman feel. Join James Moriarty and his team of misfit criminals as they try to pull off the heists of the century— all while avoiding their respective pasts, and dodging that dastardly detective, Sherlock Holmes. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information.",
